@startuml
title How a HyperCore action reaches the book, and in what order
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #4A78B5

start
:signed action arrives in the mempool
at time arrival_time;
if (what kind of action?) then (cancel)
  :f = 0, so effective_time = arrival_time.
  Cancels are never delayed by anything;<<#EAF6F0>>
elseif (ALO, post-only) then
  :treated like a cancel in the mempool:
  FIFO, no priority effect on ordering;<<#EAF6F0>>
  :any ALO priority fee instead reorders
  the queue tail at that price level,
  among orders placed in the last 400 ms;
  note right
    Charged on resting notional at
    placement, whether or not it fills
  end note
else (IOC or GTC)
  :effective_time = arrival_time + f(priority_fee)
  with f strictly decreasing, 0-8 bps linear
  at roughly 45 ms saved per basis point;
  note right
    Charged on filled notional.
    8 bps to 100% only breaks ties
    inside a 70 ms bucket
  end note
endif
:mempool sorts by effective_time,
across block boundaries;
:HyperBFT commits the block;
:execution sorts the block's actions into classes
1. no GTC/IOC order  2. cancels  3. GTC/IOC orders;
note right
  Proposer order applies only
  within a class, and the
  prioritisation spans several blocks
end note
:margin check on placement;
if (order crosses the book?) then (yes)
  if (resting order is the same address?) then (yes)
    :cancel the resting order, no fill,
    no fee, not shown in the trade feed;<<#FFF7E6>>
  else (no)
    :match at price-time priority;
    :margin check on the resting side
    for every match;
  endif
else (no)
  :rest at its price level;
endif
stop
@enduml
